          "prefix_conf_file": "etc/aiplayerbot.conf",
          "prefix_conf_key": "AiPlayerbot.RandomBotAccountPrefix",
          "registry": null
        }
      },
      "client": {
        "version": "1.12.1",
        "build": 5875,
        "notes": [
          "Community repacks (realmlist.wtf at top level, no locale folder) are detected and warned about."
        ]
      },
      "has_manifests": true
    },
    {
      "id": "wow-tortoise",
      "name": "WoW Tortoise",
      "status": "beta",
      "description": "Tortoise on the Penqle core: tortoise-wow/tortoise-wow branch bot-helpers, a MaNGOS Zero lineage, with the TortoiseBots module compiled in statically and the whole thing source-compiled in Docker. This is the tree the Turtle WoW V2 servers are built from. bot-helpers is the branch the bots module requires -- it carries the headless bot sessions (PR #438) -- and the bots themselves are Sagiroth/TortoiseBots, cloned into modules/TortoiseBots. It replaces the retired Shyalya fork that vendored the cmangos playerbots; a server already installed from that fork goes on opening, starting and being played, and is not migrated. Commands reach this world down the worldserver console the Console tab types at: the core links neither SOAP nor a telnet console (T30 Half 1, yulon-arch 2026-09-11). Driven with a real 1.18.1 client on the test box.",
      "emulator": {
        "name": "tortoise-wow/tortoise-wow @ bot-helpers (the Penqle core) + Sagiroth/TortoiseBots",
        "sources": [
          {
            "repo": "tortoise-wow/tortoise-wow",
            "branch": "bot-helpers",
            "dest": "src/tortoise-wow",
            "rev": "9980181ce9aa5940b6125a5991cc754148ed9b82"
          },
          {
            "repo": "Sagiroth/TortoiseBots",
            "branch": "main",
            "dest": "src/tortoise-wow/modules/TortoiseBots",
            "rev": "fd7ec9ec7659035cfc3ea75d542c8683005525de"
          }
        ]
      },
      "install": {
        "platforms": [
          "linux",
          "windows"
        ],
        "default_server_dir": "tortoise-wow-server",
        "requires_client_dir": true,
        "password": {
          "mode": "generated",
          "file": ".db_password",
          "prefix": "tortoise-"
        },
        "native": {
          "family": "cmangos",
          "templates": "shared/cmangos",
          "dockerfile_dir": "wow-tortoise/native",
          "image_prefix": "yulon.local/cmangos-tortoise-",
          "images": [
            "server"
          ],
          "min_ram_gb": 6,
          "warn_ram_gb": 8,
          "min_data_root_gb": 20,
          "warn_data_root_gb": 30,
          "min_server_dir_gb": 20,
          "warn_server_dir_gb": 30,
          "db": {
            "image": "mariadb:10.6",
            "client": "mariadb",
            "user": "mangos",
            "charset": "utf8mb4"
          },
          "ready": {
            "world": "World server is up and running|World initialized|MaNGOS.*started up successfully|Ready to login",
            "auth": null,
            "fatal": "Correct \\*.map files not found|Could not open (?!.*Logging to it is off for this run)|Database .* not found|\\[1146\\] Table .* doesn't exist|Your database structure is not up to date",
            "regex": true,
            "timeout_s": 10800,
            "restart_loop": 4
          },
          "cmangos": {
            "client": {
              "required_file": null,
              "min_mpq": 5,
              "mpq_depth": 2,
              "locale_mpq_required": false,
              "near_client_warn_gb": 8
            },
            "dockerfile": {
              "make_jobs": 2
            },
            "extract": {
              "image": "server",
              "ulimit_stack_unlimited": false,
              "tools": [
                {
                  "name": "maps and dbc",
                  "argv": [
                    "/opt/tortoise/bin/mapextractor",
                    "-i",
                    "/client",
                    "-o",
                    "/out",
                    "-e",
                    "3"
                  ],
                  "produces": {
                    "dbc": 100,
                    "maps": 100
                  }
                },
                {
                  "name": "vmap extract",
                  "argv": [
                    "/opt/tortoise/bin/vmapextractor",
                    "-d",
                    "/client/Data/"
                  ],
                  "produces": {
                    "Buildings": 100
                  }
                },
                {
                  "name": "vmap assemble",
                  "argv": [
                    "/opt/tortoise/bin/vmap_assembler",
                    "/out/Buildings",
                    "/out/vmaps"
                  ],
                  "produces": {
                    "vmaps": 100
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            "mmaps": {
              "argv": [
                "/opt/tortoise/bin/MoveMapGen",
                "--silent",
                "--doNotFilterDeepWater",
                "--offMeshInput",
                "/opt/tortoise/src/tools/mmap/offmesh.txt",
                "--settingsInput",
                "/opt/tortoise/src/tools/mmap/mmapSettings.txt"
              ],
              "min_files": 500,
              "required": false,
              "success_codes": [1]
            },
            "conf": {
              "source_dir": "/opt/tortoise/etc",
              "files": {
                "aiplayerbot.conf": {
                  "template": "aiplayerbot.conf",
                  "keys": {
                    "AiPlayerbot.Enabled": "1",
                    "AiPlayerbot.RandomBotAutoCreate": "1",
                    "AiPlayerbot.RandomBotAutologin": "1",
                    "AiPlayerbot.RandomBotLoginAtStartup": "1",
                    "AiPlayerbot.MinRandomBots": "500",
                    "AiPlayerbot.MaxRandomBots": "500"
                  }
                },
                "modules/tortoise_bots.conf": {
                  "template": "modules/tortoise_bots.conf.dist",
                  "keys": {
                    "TortoiseBots.AutoTest": "0",
                    "TortoiseBots.PacketBridgeTest": "0",
                    "TortoiseBots.PendingAddRemoveTest": "0",
                    "TortoiseBots.LogLevel": "1",
                    "AiPlayerbot.Observability": "0"
                  }
                },
                "mangosd.conf": {
                  "keys": {
                    "LoginDatabase.Info": "\"{{DB_HOST}};3306;{{DB_USER}};{{DB_PASSWORD}};{{AUTH_DB}}\"",
                    "WorldDatabase.Info": "\"{{DB_HOST}};3306;{{DB_USER}};{{DB_PASSWORD}};{{WORLD_DB}}\"",
                    "CharacterDatabase.Info": "\"{{DB_HOST}};3306;{{DB_USER}};{{DB_PASSWORD}};{{CHAR_DB}}\"",
                    "LogsDatabase.Info": "\"{{DB_HOST}};3306;{{DB_USER}};{{DB_PASSWORD}};{{LOGS_DB}}\"",
                    "Database.AutoUpdate.Enabled": "1",
                    "Database.AutoUpdate.Path": "\"/opt/tortoise/sql/database_updates/\"",
                    "Database.AutoUpdate.AuthUpdateName": "\"auth\"",
                    "Database.AutoUpdate.CharUpdateName": "\"character\"",
                    "Database.AutoUpdate.WorldUpdateName": "\"world\"",
                    "Database.AutoUpdate.AllowedModules": "\"all\"",
                    "Database.AutoUpdate.SortByName": "1",
                    "DataDir": "\"/opt/tortoise/data\"",
                    "WorldServerPort": "{{WORLD_PORT}}",
                    "GameType": "0",
                    "GM.LoginState": "0",
                    "GM.StartLevel": "1",
                    "AutoHonorRestart": "0",
                    "AutoRestart.MaxServerUptime": "0",
                    "Console.Enable": "1"
                  }
                },
                "realmd.conf": {
                  "keys": {
                    "LoginDatabaseInfo": "\"{{DB_HOST}};3306;{{DB_USER}};{{DB_PASSWORD}};{{AUTH_DB}}\"",
                    "ForcePinAccountRank": "10"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "sql": {
              "create": [],
              "phases": [
                {
                  "name": "schemas",
                  "files": [
                    "src/tortoise-wow/sql/create_databases.sql"
                  ],
                  "on_error": "fail"
                },
                {
                  "name": "app user and grants",
                  "statements": [
                    "CREATE USER IF NOT EXISTS '{{DB_USER}}'@'%' IDENTIFIED BY '{{DB_PASSWORD}}'",
                    "GRANT ALL ON `{{WORLD_DB}}`.* TO '{{DB_USER}}'@'%'",
                    "GRANT ALL ON `{{CHAR_DB}}`.* TO '{{DB_USER}}'@'%'",
                    "GRANT ALL ON `{{AUTH_DB}}`.* TO '{{DB_USER}}'@'%'",
                    "GRANT ALL ON `{{LOGS_DB}}`.* TO '{{DB_USER}}'@'%'",
                    "FLUSH PRIVILEGES"
                  ],
                  "on_error": "fail"
                },
                {
                  "name": "world base",
                  "into": "tw_world",
                  "files": [
                    "src/tortoise-wow/sql/base/*.sql"
                  ],
                  "sort": "name",
                  "on_error": "fail",
                  "notes": [
                    "190 per-table tw_world dumps on the pinned core, counted on yulon-arch 2026-09-11 (T30 Half 1, 06-sql-layout.txt). Unchanged from the retired fork.",
                    "THREE PHASES WERE REMOVED HERE, each naming a directory this tree does not have, all three read on the same day: `playerbots characters` and `playerbots world` globbed `modules/mod-playerbots/sql/...`, which went with the vendored cmangos playerbots, and `character updates` globbed `sql/character_updates/`, which the Penqle core has never had. The last of those was `on_error: fail`, so it would have stopped every fresh install on a directory that is simply absent.",
                    "NOTHING IN THIS PLAN IMPORTS THE BOTS' OWN SQL, and that is not an omission. The core's own updater applies module migrations at world start from `<TW_SOURCE_MODULES_DIR>/TortoiseBots/data/sql/<CharUpdateName|WorldUpdateName>` (`AutoUpdater.cpp:245-283`, `:497-531`) -- the same `character` and `world` folder names this entry's conf block writes. Measured on yulon-arch 2026-09-11: 5 character and 3 world module migrations applied at first start, and the ai_playerbot_* tables exist afterwards (Half 1 run 2, 08d/08e). The Dockerfile is what makes that compiled-in path resolve inside the runtime image; its comment says how and why.",
                    "The removed `character updates` was also the catalog's only `rerun_on_marked` phase (T11), so this plan has none. An install made from the retired fork keeps every row it already has -- that flag only ever ADDED a re-run -- and every glob this plan still carries resolves on that older tree too, so pressing Install on one refuses or proceeds by its marker exactly as before."
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "name": "realm row",
                  "into": "tw_logon",
                  "statements": [
                    "REPLACE INTO realmlist (id,name,address,port,icon,realmflags,timezone,allowedSecurityLevel,population,realmbuilds) VALUES (1, 'Tortoise WoW', '{{REALM_HOST}}', {{WORLD_PORT}}, 0,0,0,0,0, '{{CLIENT_BUILD}}')"
                  ],
                  "on_error": "fail"
                }
              ],
              "verify": [
                {
                  "db": "tw_world",
                  "query": "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema='tw_world'",
                  "min": 150
                },
                {
                  "db": "tw_logon",
                  "query": "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM realmlist",
                  "min": 1
                }
              ],
              "player_data": [
                {
                  "db": "tw_char",
                  "table": "characters"
                },
                {
                  "db": "tw_logon",
                  "table": "account",
                  "exclude_usernames": [
                    "ADMINISTRATOR",
                    "GAMEMASTER",
                    "MODERATOR",
                    "PLAYER"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "marker_db": "tw_world"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "containers": {
        "db": "tortoise-db",
        "auth": "tortoise-realmd",
        "world": "tortoise-mangosd"
      },
      "ports": {
        "auth": 3724,
        "world": 8090,
        "db": 3306
      },
      "databases": {
        "auth": "tw_logon",
        "characters": "tw_char",
        "world": "tw_world",
        "extra": [
          "tw_logs"
        ]
      },
      "realmlist": {
        "table": "realmlist",
        "address_column": "address",
        "local_address_column": null
      },
      "play": {
        "equipped": { "template_column": "item_template" },
        "teleport_command": "tele name",
        "mail_item_cap": 1,
        "revive_offline": true,
        "rename_command": "rename",
        "rename_offline_refusal": "has to be logged in before a rename can be flagged on this server -- the same command run on an offline character here replaces the name with the character's guid instead, so it is not sent",
        "set_level_command": null,
        "set_level_absent_reason": "No set-level control on this server. Nothing its console can run moves an existing character to a level you pick: `.levelup` is the one that would, and the console is not allowed to run it, while `.rndbot level <bot>` ignores the number it is handed and re-rolls that bot at the level it already has. What the console can do is `.reset level`, which puts a character who is logged in back to the configured starting level, and `.rndbot create level=<n>`, which makes a NEW character at the level you name rather than moving one that is already there."
      },
      "accounts": {
        "level": { "level_column": "rank", "max_level": 4 },
        "scheme": "mangos_sha"
      },
      "console": {
        "prompt": "mangos>",
        "prompt_precedes_answer": false
      },
      "operations": {
        "channel": "attach",
        "notes": [
          "THE PENQLE CORE HAS NO SOAP. Not the keys, not the conf block, not the subsystem: the only occurrence of the string anywhere under src/ at the pinned rev is a comment at src/game/World.h:799, no SOAP.* key is in mangosd.conf.dist.in, and no gsoap is vendored (T30 Half 1, yulon-arch 2026-09-11, 05-conf-keys.txt). What it offers instead is Console.Enable, which is the console the Console tab already types at, and an HttpApi.Enable that is not a channel kind this app knows. So this entry is back on `attach`, which is what it said until 2026-09-08 and what AttachChannel (channel.py:88-105) was written for.",
          "THE WAY BACK IS ONE EDIT OF THIS BLOCK, and the owner has asked the core's maintainer for the subsystem back. When a rev lands that carries it, restore exactly: \"channel\": \"soap\", \"namespace\": \"urn:MaNGOS\", \"port\": 7878, \"gm_level\": 4, \"publish\": true, and \"enable_conf\": {\"file\": \"etc/mangosd.conf\", \"keys\": {\"SOAP.Enabled\": \"1\", \"SOAP.IP\": \"0.0.0.0\", \"SOAP.Port\": \"7878\"}}. Those four keys plus the three SOAP.* conf keys are the whole of it on this side. Two other edits go with it and nothing else does: `_for_tortoise` in ui/controller_view.py builds a channel_setup.InstallChannel over channel.SoapChannel again instead of channel.AttachChannel, and tests/test_catalog_operations.py's Tortoise expectation flips back. No SOAP code was removed anywhere for this change -- SoapChannel, InstallChannel, the enable_conf writer in channel_setup.py and tortoise accounts' reset_own_password are all still here and still tested.",
          "The three SOAP.* keys are NOT in this entry's conf table while the channel is `attach`, because a conf key the emulator does not read is a claim that somebody measured something. They come back with the block above, as `enable_conf`, which is the only place they have ever been written from.",
          "Nothing in ready.world or ready.fatal depends on the channel: both are lines the worldserver prints on its own stdout, read by the install spine before any channel exists."
        ]
      },
      "observability": {
        "characters": {
          "table": "characters",
          "account": "account",
          "online": "online"
        },
        "bots": {
          "account_prefix": "rndbot",
          "prefix_conf_file": "etc/aiplayerbot.conf",
          "prefix_conf_key": "AiPlayerbot.RandomBotAccountPrefix",
          "registry": null
        }
      },
      "client": {
        "version": "1.18.1",
        "build": 7272,
        "notes": [
          "Only the custom Turtle-WoW 1.18.1 client (build 7272) works; any other build will not connect."
        ]
      },
      "has_manifests": true
    }
  ]
}
